0..79 Comment "/// A transport whose motive starts at another point than its moved path prints"
80..107 Comment "/// as the transport it is."
108..111 Comment "///"
112..193 Comment "/// A transport along `r` of `Path.here(f)`, under a motive `Path[.A = C](l, c)`,"
194..268 Comment "/// is the composite `Path.step(Path.here(f), r)` exactly when `l` is `f`."
269..346 Comment "/// Reading that composite back takes the motive\'s start from `Path.here(f)`."
347..420 Comment "/// A motive that starts at `Path.step(f, Path.here(z))` is another type,"
421..460 Comment "/// which the composite does not spell."
461..464 Comment "///"
465..542 Comment "/// The printer writes a transport as a composite only where the moved path\'s"
543..612 Comment "/// start is the motive\'s. Otherwise it writes the transport in full."
613..616 Comment "///"
617..688 Comment "/// - see: #4218 — the printer wrote both transports as one composite"
689..759 Comment "/// - see: #754 — a returned composite of paths is written as a step"
761..836 Comment "/// Motives whose fixed starts differ by the right unit of a variable path."
